# Build context is the repo root (the Dockerfile does COPY backend/...).
# Everything the image does not need stays out: a fat context is slow to upload
# on every deploy, and secrets that never enter the context cannot leak from a
# layer.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Secrets — belt and braces. These are gitignored too.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# Agent + editor scratch
AGENTS.md
NOTES.local.md
.claude/
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python build junk
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# The frontend IS built inside this image (see infra/Dockerfile's `web` stage),
# so the sources must reach the build context. Only the heavy derived
# directories are excluded — npm ci regenerates node_modules in the stage.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# Local data must never be baked into an image
.data/
.run/
*.db
*.sqlite3

# Docs. Deliberately NOT a blanket *.md rule: backend/skills/*/SKILL.md IS the
# skills content, and excluding it makes skills_engine index 0 in the container
# while working perfectly on a laptop — every turn then silently loses its skill
# blocks. A few KB of stray markdown in the image is the cheaper mistake.
docs/
